INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:barnet/barnet-1471:occurred','episode','barnet/barnet-1471','Battle of Barnet','barnet','occurred',1471,1471,'Battle of Barnet','Easter Sunday, 14 April 1471 (Julian calendar; 23 April by the modern calendar). Secure. Edward reached Barnet on the evening of 13 April and deployed in the dark; the Arrivall says the fight began between four and five in the morning and lasted about three hours, Warkworth from four until ten.',NULL,NULL,'attested-documentary','medium','bar-barnet-battlefield-project-2015-2018,bar-watson-2022-looking-for-the-site,bar-battlefields-trust-barnet,bar-arrivall-part-3,bar-warkworth-barnet,bar-barnet-society-2021,bar-barnet-museum-battle',7,'locations/barnet/episodes.json','$[0]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:brentford/brentford-1016:occurred','episode','brentford/brentford-1016','Battle of Brentford','brentford','occurred',1016,1016,'Battle of Brentford','1016; day and month not recorded. In the Chronicle it comes ''within two nights'' of Edmund''s relief of London, after Cnut''s siege had begun in May and after Edmund''s fights at Penselwood and Sherston, and before the battle of Assandun and Edmund''s death on St Andrew''s day (30 November). Summer is likely but is an inference.',NULL,NULL,'attested-documentary','medium','bre-asc-avalon,bre-vch-mdx7-growth,bre-vch-mdx7-comms,bre-clerk-siege-london,bre-bclhs-brentford-bridge,bre-wheeler-old-england,bre-wikipedia-battle',7,'locations/brentford/episodes.json','$[0]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:london/boudica-60:occurred','episode','london/boudica-60','Boudica''s sack of Londinium','london','occurred',60,60,'Boudica''s sack of Londinium','AD 60 or 61; season unknown. Tacitus puts the revolt under the consuls Caesennius Paetus and Petronius Turpilianus (the consuls of AD 61), but many scholars prefer 60 on the grounds that the events need more than one year. The RCHME volume on Roman London prefers 60; MOLA writes ''AD 60/61''. A Bloomberg writing tablet dated 21 October AD 62 shows London trading again by then, which fits either year. Use 60 with a visible ''or 61''.',NULL,NULL,'attested-excavated','high','ev-tacitus-annals-book-xiv-chapters-29-39-loeb-tran,ev-cassius-dio-roman-history-epitome-of-book-lxii-l,ev-introduction-london-in-a-d-60-in-an-inventory-of,ev-a-research-framework-for-london-archaeology-2002,ev-roman-fort-built-in-response-to-boudica-s-uprisi,ev-bloomberg-writing-tablets-contract-of-21-october,ev-letters-from-londinium,ev-ad-50-the-story-of-roman-london,ev-london-s-catastrophic-fires,ev-boudica-s-revolt-and-the-sack-of-london-secondar',10,'locations/london/episodes.json','$[0]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:london/london-bridge-1014:occurred','episode','london/london-bridge-1014','Battle of London Bridge','london','occurred',1014,1014,'Battle of London Bridge','Uncertain. Snorri places it after Swein Forkbeard''s death (February 1014) as part of Aethelred''s return, hence the usual ''1014''; Hagland and Watson accept 1014 following Ian Howard''s chronology. Olaf''s early career is poorly dated and he is also associated with Thorkell''s army, which attacked London unsuccessfully in 1009-10, so some place his London fighting then, and on the Danish side. The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle for 1014 says only that Aethelred came home in Lent and was gladly received.',NULL,NULL,'conjectural','low','ev-fact-or-folklore-the-viking-attack-on-london-bri,ev-heimskringla-saga-of-olaf-haraldson-chapter-on-t,ev-olaf-haraldsson-encyclopaedia-romana,ev-the-anglo-saxon-chronicle-eleventh-century-entri,ev-tooley-street-delight-19-march-2022-sigvatr-s-st',5,'locations/london/episodes.json','$[1]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:london/brentford-1016:occurred','episode','london/brentford-1016','Battle of Brentford','london','occurred',1016,1016,'Battle of Brentford','Summer 1016; day and month not recorded. In the Chronicle''s sequence it follows Cnut''s siege of London (begun about May), Edmund''s fights at Penselwood and Sherston (after midsummer) and his relief of London, with Brentford ''two days'' after the relief. It precedes Assandun (18 October 1016).',NULL,NULL,'attested-documentary','medium','ev-the-anglo-saxon-chronicle-eleventh-century-entry,ev-the-danish-conquest-part-10-the-siege-of-london-,ev-ealing-and-brentford-growth-of-brentford-in-a-hi,ev-fact-or-folklore-the-viking-attack-on-london-bri',4,'locations/london/episodes.json','$[2]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:london/barnet-1471:occurred','episode','london/barnet-1471','Battle of Barnet','london','occurred',1471,1471,'Battle of Barnet','Easter Sunday, 14 April 1471 (Julian calendar). Secure. Edward left London about 4 pm on 13 April and deployed in the dark; fighting began around dawn. Warkworth says about 4 am to 10 am; other accounts imply a shorter fight.',NULL,NULL,'attested-documentary','medium','ev-the-barnet-battlefield-project-2015-2018-g-foard,ev-looking-for-the-site-of-the-battle-of-barnet-b-w,ev-mystery-remains-over-lost-battlefield-site-of-14,ev-warkworth-s-chronicle-the-battle-of-barnet-text-,ev-how-much-ancient-divisions-survive-unnatural-all,ev-the-battle-of-barnet-and-the-great-north-road-se',6,'locations/london/episodes.json','$[3]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:stonehenge/stonehenge-midsummer-sunrise-2500bce:occurred','episode','stonehenge/stonehenge-midsummer-sunrise-2500bce','Midsummer sunrise along the axis, c. 2500 BCE','stonehenge','occurred',-2500,-2500,'Midsummer sunrise along the axis, c. 2500 BCE','Late June (about 21 June by the solar year) in the sarsen-circle era. The year is a representative one inside 2580 to 2400 BCE; the day is the solstice by astronomy, not a recorded date.',NULL,NULL,'reconstructed','medium','sto-darvill-2012-remodelled,sto-skyatnight-astronomy,sto-wiki-archaeoastronomy,sto-osm-overpass,sto-wikipedia-heel-stone,sto-ea-survey-2010',6,'locations/stonehenge/episodes.json','$[0]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:stonehenge/stonehenge-midwinter-sunset-2500bce:occurred','episode','stonehenge/stonehenge-midwinter-sunset-2500bce','Midwinter sunset through the Great Trilithon, c. 2500 BCE','stonehenge','occurred',-2500,-2500,'Midwinter sunset through the Great Trilithon, c. 2500 BCE','Late December (about 21 December by the solar year) in the sarsen-circle era; a representative year inside 2580 to 2400 BCE, the day fixed by astronomy.',NULL,NULL,'reconstructed','medium','sto-darvill-2012-remodelled,sto-skyatnight-astronomy,sto-wiki-archaeoastronomy,sto-osm-overpass,sto-wp-durrington',5,'locations/stonehenge/episodes.json','$[1]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:stonehenge/stonehenge-raising-sarsens:occurred','episode','stonehenge/stonehenge-raising-sarsens','Raising the sarsens','stonehenge','occurred',-2500,-2500,'Raising the sarsens','c. 2560 to 2470 BCE in the model; the sarsen circle is dated 2580 to 2475 BCE and the trilithons 2585 to 2400 BCE (93%) by the English Heritage Bayesian model. The day is arbitrary.',NULL,NULL,'reconstructed','medium','sto-darvill-2012-remodelled,sto-marshall-2012-eh-chronology,sto-eh-stones,sto-eh-research,sto-wiki-stonehenge,sto-banton-2014-abstract',6,'locations/stonehenge/episodes.json','$[2]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:stonehenge/durrington-midwinter-feast-2500bce:occurred','episode','stonehenge/durrington-midwinter-feast-2500bce','Midwinter feasting at Durrington Walls, c. 2500 BCE','stonehenge','occurred',-2500,-2500,'Midwinter feasting at Durrington Walls, c. 2500 BCE','Late December in a representative year of the village''s decade or so of use (c. 2515 to 2480 BCE in the model). The village is dated 2600 to 2500 BCE (2007 release) and, by later modelling, to roughly 10 to 12 years ending 2500 to 2460 BCE.',NULL,NULL,'reconstructed','medium','sto-bristol-2007,sto-archco-durrington,sto-wp-durrington,sto-skyatnight-astronomy,sto-wiki-archaeoastronomy',5,'locations/stonehenge/episodes.json','$[3]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:stonehenge/bush-barrow-burial:occurred','episode','stonehenge/bush-barrow-burial','Bush Barrow burial, c. 1900 BCE','stonehenge','occurred',-1900,-1900,'Bush Barrow burial, c. 1900 BCE','Wikipedia gives c. 1950 BCE for the burial and the Wilsford G7 group 2000 to 1800 BCE; 1900 BCE is a display year inside the uncertainty.',NULL,NULL,'attested-excavated','medium','sto-wp-bushbarrow,sto-wikipedia-bush-barrow,sto-wp-normanton,sto-wikipedia-normanton-down,sto-osm-overpass',5,'locations/stonehenge/episodes.json','$[4]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:stonehenge/amesbury-abbey-979:occurred','episode','stonehenge/amesbury-abbey-979','Amesbury Abbey founded, 979','stonehenge','occurred',979,979,'Amesbury Abbey founded, 979','c. 979. The foundation date is approximate; the day is arbitrary.',NULL,NULL,'attested-documentary','medium','sto-wp-amesburyabbey,sto-wp-amesbury,sto-wikipedia-amesbury-abbey,sto-osm-overpass',4,'locations/stonehenge/episodes.json','$[5]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:stonehenge/inigo-jones-survey-1620:occurred','episode','stonehenge/inigo-jones-survey-1620','Inigo Jones surveys Stonehenge for James I, 1620','stonehenge','occurred',1620,1620,'Inigo Jones surveys Stonehenge for James I, 1620','1620; the fraction 0.6 is an arbitrary display value, no month is known from the sources read. The survey and the Duke of Buckingham''s digging are both given as 1620, though English Heritage also says ''the 1620s''.',NULL,NULL,'attested-documentary','medium','sto-eh-sources,sto-eh-research,sto-webb-1655-stone-heng,sto-darvill-2012-remodelled,sto-wiki-stonehenge',5,'locations/stonehenge/episodes.json','$[6]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:stonehenge/robin-hoods-ball-3550bce:occurred','episode','stonehenge/robin-hoods-ball-3550bce','Robin Hood''s Ball causewayed enclosure, c. 3550 BCE','stonehenge','occurred',-3550,-3550,'Robin Hood''s Ball causewayed enclosure, c. 3550 BCE','''Centuries around 3500 BC'' (English Heritage); Wikipedia: probably built c. 4000 BC, possibly used to c. 3000 BC. Low confidence.',NULL,NULL,'attested-excavated','low','sto-wp-robinhood,sto-eh-history,sto-wikipedia-robin-hoods-ball',3,'locations/stonehenge/episodes.json','$[7]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:barnet/barnet-1471:located_at','episode','barnet/barnet-1471','Battle of Barnet','barnet','located_at',NULL,NULL,'Battle of Barnet','The point given is the road fork at Hadley Highstone, between the registered area (Hadley Green) and the Kitts End alternative. Treat it as the middle of a zone of possibility, not a site.',51.6655,-0.199,'attested-documentary','medium','bar-barnet-battlefield-project-2015-2018,bar-watson-2022-looking-for-the-site,bar-battlefields-trust-barnet,bar-arrivall-part-3,bar-warkworth-barnet,bar-barnet-society-2021,bar-barnet-museum-battle',7,'locations/barnet/episodes.json','$[0]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:brentford/brentford-1016:located_at','episode','brentford/brentford-1016','Battle of Brentford','brentford','located_at',NULL,NULL,'Battle of Brentford',NULL,51.4803,-0.3022,'attested-documentary','medium','bre-asc-avalon,bre-vch-mdx7-growth,bre-vch-mdx7-comms,bre-clerk-siege-london,bre-bclhs-brentford-bridge,bre-wheeler-old-england,bre-wikipedia-battle',7,'locations/brentford/episodes.json','$[0]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:london/boudica-60:located_at','episode','london/boudica-60','Boudica''s sack of Londinium','london','located_at',NULL,NULL,'Boudica''s sack of Londinium','Site well known in general, not in detail. The pre-revolt town lay on the eastern hill (Cornhill) between the Walbrook and the area north of the bridgehead, with some occupation west of the Walbrook and a suburb at the south end of the bridge in Southwark. The burnt horizon has been recorded on many City sites (King William Street, Lombard Street, Eastcheap, Miles Lane, Fenchurch Street, the Walbrook west bank) and beside the road at the Southwark bridgehead. The point given is an approximate centre of the early town, not a find spot.',51.5115,-0.0865,'attested-excavated','high','ev-tacitus-annals-book-xiv-chapters-29-39-loeb-tran,ev-cassius-dio-roman-history-epitome-of-book-lxii-l,ev-introduction-london-in-a-d-60-in-an-inventory-of,ev-a-research-framework-for-london-archaeology-2002,ev-roman-fort-built-in-response-to-boudica-s-uprisi,ev-bloomberg-writing-tablets-contract-of-21-october,ev-letters-from-londinium,ev-ad-50-the-story-of-roman-london,ev-london-s-catastrophic-fires,ev-boudica-s-revolt-and-the-sack-of-london-secondar',10,'locations/london/episodes.json','$[0]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:london/london-bridge-1014:located_at','episode','london/london-bridge-1014','Battle of London Bridge','london','located_at',NULL,NULL,'Battle of London Bridge','The place is known; the event is not. A timber bridge existed by about 1000 (first phase built of timber felled c. 987-1032) on roughly the line of the later medieval bridge, a little downstream of the present London Bridge, with Southwark at its south end. The point given is approximate mid-river on that line.',51.5079,-0.0868,'conjectural','low','ev-fact-or-folklore-the-viking-attack-on-london-bri,ev-heimskringla-saga-of-olaf-haraldson-chapter-on-t,ev-olaf-haraldsson-encyclopaedia-romana,ev-the-anglo-saxon-chronicle-eleventh-century-entri,ev-tooley-street-delight-19-march-2022-sigvatr-s-st',5,'locations/london/episodes.json','$[1]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:london/brentford-1016:located_at','episode','london/brentford-1016','Battle of Brentford','london','located_at',NULL,NULL,'Battle of Brentford','Poorly known. The Chronicle says only that Edmund crossed the Thames at Brentford. The Victoria County History notes the place-name is usually taken to mean the ford over the Brent, though a Thames crossing is possible, and that stakes on the foreshore at ''Old England'' (near the Brent-Thames confluence, by Syon) may have defended a ford; it places the 1016 fight on the south bank. The point given is the approximate Brent-Thames confluence and is a placeholder, not a located battlefield. No archaeology of the battle is known.',51.4805,-0.3075,'attested-documentary','medium','ev-the-anglo-saxon-chronicle-eleventh-century-entry,ev-the-danish-conquest-part-10-the-siege-of-london-,ev-ealing-and-brentford-growth-of-brentford-in-a-hi,ev-fact-or-folklore-the-viking-attack-on-london-bri',4,'locations/london/episodes.json','$[2]');
INSERT INTO "fact"("fact_id","entity_type","entity_id","entity_name","location_id","kind","year_from","year_to","value_text","detail","lat","lon","evidence","confidence","source_ids","n_sources","origin_file","origin_path") VALUES('episode:london/barnet-1471:located_at','episode','london/barnet-1471','Battle of Barnet','london','located_at',NULL,NULL,'Battle of Barnet','The general area is certain (north of High Barnet along the old St Albans road); the exact battlefield is not. English Heritage registered a battlefield in 1995 centred on Hadley Green / Monken Hadley, following a National Army Museum report. The 2015-18 Barnet Battlefield Project (University of Huddersfield, with the Battlefields Trust and Barnet Museum) concluded ''we cannot accurately identify the battlefield'': sources agree it lay between half a mile and a mile north of the town, the terrain of the former Kicks End (Kitts End) Common about 1.9 km north of the Barnet boundary best fits them, and Hadley Green is ''problematic''; but metal-detecting found no conclusive battle scatter. Watson (2022) gives the current best guess as a circle of 1 km radius centred on Kitts End. The point given is near Hadley Highstone, between the registered area and Kitts End; treat it as the middle of a zone roughly 2 km long, not a site.',51.668,-0.199,'attested-documentary','medium','ev-the-barnet-battlefield-project-2015-2018-g-foard,ev-looking-for-the-site-of-the-battle-of-barnet-b-w,ev-mystery-remains-over-lost-battlefield-site-of-14,ev-warkworth-s-chronicle-the-battle-of-barnet-text-,ev-how-much-ancient-divisions-survive-unnatural-all,ev-the-battle-of-barnet-and-the-great-north-road-se',6,'locations/london/episodes.json','$[3]');
